{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-28-Oct-2022-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "A man invested Rs.96,000 at the rate of 20% per annum, compounded half-yearly for 1 year. What would be 80% of the amount (in Rs.) which he will get on maturity?", "options": [{"text": "98,922", "added": false}, {"text": "92,928", "added": false}, {"text": "1,09,856", "added": false}, {"text": "1,16,160", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Two concentric circles are of radius 12 cm and r cm, respectively, where r > 12 cm. A chord of the larger circle of length 32 cm touches the smaller circle. Find the radius r?", "options": [{"text": "12 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "20 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "16 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The average of five consecutive even numbers is 66. Find the difference between the highest and the lowest numbers.", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "In a manufacturing plant, Jack, Smith and Annie can do a job of manufacturing plates in 15, 20 and 30 days, respectively. In how many days can they finish the work together?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "65°", "added": false}, {"text": "62°", "added": false}, {"text": "56°", "added": false}, {"text": "51°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Ramesh sold his bike for ₹16,384 and incurred a loss of 20%. At what price should he have sold the bike to gain a profit of 30%?", "options": [{"text": "₹27,824", "added": false}, {"text": "₹26,724", "added": false}, {"text": "₹26,624", "added": false}, {"text": "₹26,800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Permutation and Combination", "sub": "combinations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "A can do a work in 8 days and B in 12 days. If they work together on it for 3 days, then the fraction of the work that is left is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "A person P purchases a washing machine for Rs.22,000 cash or for Rs.9,000 cash down payment and two monthly instalments of Rs.8,000 each. The rate of the simple interest is:", "options": [{"text": "215%", "added": false}, {"text": "240%", "added": false}, {"text": "250%", "added": false}, {"text": "200%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "234", "added": false}, {"text": "220", "added": false}, {"text": "254", "added": false}, {"text": "184", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The list price of an article is Rs.1,200. If it is available on a discount series of 10%, 8% and 5%, the selling price of the article is:", "options": [{"text": "Rs.812.76", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.943.92", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,080.00", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.993.60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2171", "added": false}, {"text": "928", "added": false}, {"text": "1243", "added": false}, {"text": "315", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "The price of an A.C. is first increased by 16%, and later on, the price is decreased by 22% due to reduction in sales. Find the net percentage change in final price of the A.C.", "options": [{"text": "Decrease of 19.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decrease of 9.52%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase of 9.52%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase of 19.25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The radius of a roller is 56 cm and its length is 240 cm. It takes 875 complete revolutions to move once over to the level of a playground. Find the area of the playground.", "options": [{"text": "7392 m2", "added": false}, {"text": "8400 m2", "added": false}, {"text": "6389 m2", "added": false}, {"text": "7650 m2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Two trains start at the same time from stations P and Q, 1800 km apart, and proceed towards each other at an average speed of 108 km/h and 92km/h, respectively. The trains will meet at:", "options": [{"text": "828 km from station P", "added": false}, {"text": "972 km from station Q", "added": false}, {"text": "540 km from Station Q", "added": false}, {"text": "972 km from station P", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "In ∆ABC, LB = 90° and BD ⟂ AC. If AC = 9 cm and AD = 3 cm, then BD is equal to:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A radii of the bases of the two cylinders are in the ratio 5 : 7 and their height are in the ratio 3 : 5. Find the ratio of their curved surface areas.", "options": [{"text": "9 : 8", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "C", "added": false}, {"text": "D", "added": false}, {"text": "E", "added": false}, {"text": "B", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "Ram, Shyam and Ghanshyam have ₹32, ₹46 and ₹50, respectively, with them. Their mother asks them to give her equal amounts so that the money held by them now are in continued proportion. Find the amount taken from each of them.", "options": [{"text": "₹91.36", "added": false}, {"text": "₹51.78", "added": false}, {"text": "₹91.78", "added": false}, {"text": "₹51.60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "polynomials-and-factorisation", "key_answer": null}]}